ics","drugs":[{"n":"Amphetamine","d":"5–15 mg oral"},"Fenfluramine","Dexfenfluramine",{"n":"Sibutramine","d":"Start with 10 mg OD, increase to 15 mg OD if needed"}]},{"name":"Uterine relaxants","drugs":[{"n":"Ritodrine","d":"50–200 µg/min i.v. infusion, 10 mg i.m./oral 4–6 hourly","b":"Yutopar, Ritrod, Ritodine"},{"n":"Isoxsuprine","d":"5–10 mg oral, i.m. 4–6 hourly","b":"Duvadilan"},{"n":"Salbutamol","d":"2–4 mg oral, 0.25–0.5 mg i.m./s.c., 100–200 µg by inhalation","b":"Asthalin, Croysal, Salol, Ventorlin"},{"n":"Terbutaline","d":"5 mg oral, 0.25 mg s.c., 250 µg by inhalation","b":"Bricarex, Misthaler, Bricanyl"}]}]}},{"id":"alpha-adrenergic-blocking-drugs","title":"Alpha adrenergic blocking drugs","root":{"name":"α ADRENERGIC BLOCKING DRUGS","children":[{"name":"Non equilibrium type","children":[{"name":"β-haloalkylamine","drugs":[{"n":"Phenoxybenzamine","d":"20–60 mg/day oral, 1 mg/kg slow i.v. infusion over 1 hour","b":"Fenoxene, Biophenox"}]}]},{"name":"Equilibrium type (Competitive antagonists)","children":[{"name":"Non selective","children":[{"name":"Ergot alkaloids","drugs":[{"n":"Ergotamine","d":"For migraine 1–3 mg oral/sublingual, repeat as required (max 6 mg in a day); rarely 0.25–0.5 mg i.m. or s.c","b":"Gynergen, Ingagen"},"Ergotoxine"]},{"name":"Hydrogenated ergot alkaloids","drugs":[{"n":"Dihydroergotamine (DHE)","d":"For migraine 2–6 mg oral (max 10 mg/day), 0.5–1 mg i.m., s.c. repeat hourly (max 3 mg)","b":"Dihydergot, DHE, Migranil"},{"n":"Dihydroergotoxine (Codergocrine)","d":"For dementia 1–1.5 mg oral or sublingual, 0.15–0.6 mg i.m","b":"Hydergine, Cereloid"}]},{"name":"Imidazoline","drugs":[{"n":"Phentolamine","d":"5 mg i.v. repeated as required","b":"Regitine, Fentanor"}]},{"name":"Miscellaneous","drugs":["Chlorpromazine"]}]},{"name":"α1 Selective","drugs":[{"n":"Prazosin","d":"Start with 0.5–1 mg at bedtime; usual dose 1–4 mg BD or TDS","b":"Prazopres, Minipress"},{"n":"Terazosin","d":"Usual maintenance dose 2–10 mg OD","b":"Hytrin, Teralfa